Troubleshoot and resolve a Docker Compose network isolation issue where the service container is unreachable by its IP address from the host.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find `app.py`, `Dockerfile`, and `docker-compose.yml`.
- Start the Compose services (`docker compose up -d` or `docker-compose up -d`).
- Inspect the container's IP address (`docker inspect unreachable_web_app --format='{{range .NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{.IPAddress}}{{end}}'`).
- Attempting to ping or connect to the container IP address (e.g. `curl http://<container_ip>:8080`) fails because the network is completely isolated from the host.
- Diagnose why the container network blocks host routing:
  - Inspect `docker-compose.yml`.
  - Notice `networks.isolated_net` has `internal: true` enabled, restricting external network access.
- Update `/app/docker-compose.yml` to remove `internal: true` (or set `internal: false`).
- Re-run `docker compose up -d`.
- Verify that connecting to the container IP address (`curl http://<container_ip>:8080`) returns `OK - Service Accessible`.
